{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-4890-b1c2-d3e4f5a67890",
    "name": "TCSS-460 Message API - Random Data Generator",
    "description": "Random data generation collection for the TCSS-460 Message API using Postman's dynamic variables.\n\n**Features:**\n- Uses Postman's built-in random variables (`$randomFirstName`, `$randomPhrase`, etc.)\n- Custom random priority generator (1-3)\n- Perfect for quickly populating the database with test data\n- Collection variables store generated data for reference\n\n**Setup Instructions:**\n1. Import this collection into Postman\n2. Create an environment with variable `baseUrl` set to `http://localhost:8000`\n3. Run 'Generate API Key' request first to get authentication token\n4. Use the 'Quick DB Population' folder to rapidly create random messages\n5. Run individual requests or use Collection Runner for bulk data generation\n\n**Usage Tips:**\n- The 'Create Random Message' request can be run multiple times to populate DB\n- Each run generates completely new random data\n- Use Collection Runner with iterations for bulk population (e.g., 50 iterations = 50 random messages)\n- Random priority is generated via pre-request script (1, 2, or 3)",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Collection-level random priority generator",
          "// Generates random priority value: 1, 2, or 3",
          "function getRandomPriority() {",
          "    return Math.floor(Math.random() * 3) + 1;",
          "}",
          "",
          "// Store random priority in collection variable for use in requests",
          "pm.collectionVariables.set('randomPriority', getRandomPriority());",
          "",
          "// Optional delay between requests (useful for Collection Runner)",
          "const delayMs = pm.collectionVariables.get('requestDelay') || 0;",
          "if (delayMs > 0) {",
          "    console.log(`⏱️ Waiting ${delayMs}ms before request...`);",
          "    setTimeout(function(){}, delayMs);",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Log test results summary",
          "const testResults = pm.response.code;",
          "console.log(`✓ ${pm.info.requestName} - Status: ${testResults}`);"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "apiKey",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "randomPriority",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Auto-generated random priority (1-3) - updated before each request"
    },
    {
      "key": "lastCreatedName",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Stores the last randomly generated name for reference"
    },
    {
      "key": "requestDelay",
      "value": "0",
      "type": "number",
      "description": "Delay in milliseconds between requests (0 = no delay, 500 = half second)"
    }
  ],
